          "settings": {
            "tabs": [
              {
                "tab_title": "Which path should a complete beginner start with?",
                "tab_content": "Start with Foundations Path first. It gives you the Python, SQL and mental model needed to understand why the later paths exist and how they connect.",
                "_id": "000019a"
              },
              {
                "tab_title": "Can I jump straight to orchestration or streaming?",
                "tab_content": "Yes, if you already have strong fundamentals. For most learners, the roadmap should remain the default because orchestration and streaming are easier when storage and transformation already make sense.",
                "_id": "000019b"
              },
              {
                "tab_title": "Do I need to finish every path in strict order?",
                "tab_content": "No. The roadmap is a recommended sequence, not a prison. It is still the best default because each path removes confusion for the one that follows.",
                "_id": "000019c"
              },
              {
                "tab_title": "How do courses, labs and quizzes work together?",
                "tab_content": "Courses provide structure, labs create repetition and quizzes validate the concepts. The path page should connect all three so learners feel one system instead of three disconnected surfaces.",
                "_id": "000019d"
              }
            ],
